course: dictionary
lesson: 6907
title: Oxbow lakes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A river often winds in loops called meanders. Sometimes the river cuts straight through the narrow neck of a loop and leaves the loop behind. «An oxbow lake forms when a river cuts through the narrow neck of a meander and leaves the loop behind.» So an oxbow lake is a curved lake that was once part of the river.
explain: Read the clues: a loop, a neck, a river, left behind. The second sentence says the same idea in other words: «If it cuts across the neck of a loop, the old loop is left behind as an oxbow lake.» Two sentences, one meaning. Check it by putting your own meaning into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
explain: The word oxbow has other meanings too. It can mean a big U-shaped bend in a river. It can also mean a wooden collar that fits around an ox's neck. In a geography lesson, the lake meaning is the one you need, so look at the words around it to choose.
fact: An oxbow lake is a curved lake.
fact: It forms when a river cuts off a loop, called a meander.
fact: A meander is a bend or loop in a river.
fact: An oxbow is also a big U-shaped bend in a river.
fact: An oxbow can also be a U-shaped wooden collar that fits around an ox's neck to fix it to a yoke.
exercise: «An oxbow lake forms when a river cuts through the narrow neck of a meander.» What does an oxbow lake form from? | A tall hill beside the sea | *A loop of river cut off from the main river | A waterfall over rocks | A lake made by rain in a field
exercise: What is a meander? | *A bend or loop in a river | A deep, still pond on a hill | A bridge over the water | A wooden collar for an ox
exercise: «The old loop is left behind as an oxbow lake.» What does left behind suggest? | *It has been cut off and is no longer part of the main river | It has been moved to a new place | It is still joined to the river at both ends | It has grown much bigger
test: Which word means a bend or loop in a river? | Oxbow lake | Yoke | Neck | *Meander
test: What does a wooden oxbow collar fit around? | *An ox's neck | A hill's top | A river's mouth | A lake's edge
exam: A river loop has been cut off and left behind as a curved lake. What is this lake called? | A flood plain | A waterfall | *An oxbow lake | A delta
